WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.120
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.720
Today we are going to not only simulate fluids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:14.800
but even better, we're going to absorb&nbsp;
them with sponge-like porous materials too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:21.040
This paper does not have the usual super high&nbsp;
resolution results that you see with many other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:27.520
simulation papers. However, I really wanted&nbsp;
to show you what it can do through four lovely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:33.920
experiments. And, at the end of the episode,&nbsp;
you will see how slowly or quickly it runs!

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:42.640
Experiment number one. Spongy dumbbells. One side&nbsp;
is made of a spongy material, and if it starts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:50.480
absorbing the water, let’s see if it sinks. Well,&nbsp;
it slowly starts to descend as it gets heavier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:57.840
and then, it gets so heavy that eventually, it&nbsp;
sinks the other half too. That is a good start.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:05.040
Now, experiment number two. Absorption.&nbsp;
Here, the green liquid is hard to absorb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.880
therefore we expect it to pass through.&nbsp;
While the red liquid is easier to absorb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:18.080
and should get stuck in this perforated material.&nbsp;
Let’s see if that is indeed what happens…the green&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:24.720
is coming through, and where is all the red&nbsp;
goo? Well, most of it is getting absorbed here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:31.680
But wait, the paper promises to ensure that&nbsp;
mass and momentum still gets transferred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:37.200
through the interactions properly. So, if&nbsp;
the fluid volumes are simulated correctly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:44.640
we expect a lot more green down there than&nbsp;
red. Did we get it? Oh yes, checkmark!

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:48.560
And if you think this was a&nbsp;
great absorption simulation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:54.960
wait until you see this. Experiment&nbsp;
number three. Absorption on steroids.&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:02.960
This is a liquid mixture, and these are porous&nbsp;
materials. Each of which will absorb exactly one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:09.200
component of the liquid and let through&nbsp;
the rest. Let’s see…the first obstacle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:16.080
absorbs the blue component quickly, the second&nbsp;
retains all the green component, and the red&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:24.640
flows through. And, look at how gracefully&nbsp;
the red fluid fills the last sponge. Lovely.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:31.840
Onwards to experiment number four. Artistic&nbsp;
control. Since we are building our own little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:37.680
virtual world, we make all the rules.&nbsp;
So let’s see the first absorption case.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:43.760
Nothing too crazy here. But, if this is&nbsp;
not in line with our artistic vision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:49.840
do not despair, because this is our world, so&nbsp;
we can play with these physical parameters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:56.160
For instance, let’s increase the absorption&nbsp;
rate, so that the fluid enters the solid faster.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:05.680
Or, we can increase the permeability, this is the&nbsp;
ease of passage of the fluid through the material.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.000
Does it transfer quicker into the sponge?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:17.200
Yes it does! And finally, we can speed up&nbsp;
both how quickly the fluid enters the solid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.800
how quickly it travels within, and we have&nbsp;
also increased the amount of absorption.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:30.240
Let’s see if we end up with a smaller remaining&nbsp;
volume. Indeed we do! The beauty of building these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:35.440
virtual worlds is that we can have these&nbsp;
simulations under our artistic control.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:42.480
So, how long do we wait for the sponges? Well,&nbsp;
hold on to your papers, because we not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:48.960
don’t have to sit down and watch an episode of&nbsp;
Spongebob to get these done, but… get this. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:55.920
crazy three-sponge experiment used about quarter&nbsp;
of a million particles for the fluid, and another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:02.320
quarter-ish million particles for the solids,&nbsp;
and runs at approximately a second per frame.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:08.720
Yes, it runs interactively, and all&nbsp;
this on a consumer graphics card.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:15.360
And, yes, so that’s why the resolution of the&nbsp;
simulations is not that high. The authors could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:21.680
have posted a much higher resolution simulation&nbsp;
and kept the execution time in the minutes per&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:29.040
frame domain, but no. They wanted to show us&nbsp;
what this can do interactively. And in this case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:35.520
it is important that you apply the First Law Of&nbsp;
Papers, which says that research is a process.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:42.880
Do not look at where we are, look at where we will&nbsp;
be two more papers down the line. So, there we go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:48.480
I really wanted to show you this paper, because&nbsp;
unfortunately, if we don’t talk about it, almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:55.440
no one will see it. This is why Two Minute Papers&nbsp;
exists. And, if you wish to discuss this paper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.560
make sure to drop by on our Discord server.&nbsp;
The link is available in the video description.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:50.400
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

